{{also|Machete}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Machette_kos.pg.jpg|thumb|right|250px|a machete]]

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|es|machete}}, diminutive of {{m|es|macho||sledgehammer}}, from {{der|en|la|mattea}}, possibly from {{m|la|mactare||slaughter in sacrifice}}; cognate with {{cog|fro|machier}}, {{cog|fr|massue}}, English {{m|fr|mace}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/məˈʃɛ.ti/|/məˈtʃɛ.ti/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-ncalif-machete.ogg|Audio (US, Northern California)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[sword]]-like [[tool]] used for [[cut]]ting large [[plant]]s with a [[chop]]ping motion, or as a [[weapon]]. The blade is usually 50 to 65 centimeters long, and up to three millimeters thick.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|bolo}}
* {{l|en|sundang}}

